     C*
     C* Embedded SQL in RPG/400. EXEC SQL occupies positions 8-16 with
     C* a slash in 7; the statement runs from 17 to 74. Continuation
     C* lines carry + in position 7 and text from position 9.
     C*
     C* Member: RPGSQL   Compilable: no (calculations only, no files)
     C* Source: IBM i 7.5 Embedded SQL programming, coding SQL
     C*         statements in RPG/400 applications.
     C* Retrieved: 2026-07-26
     C*
     C*
     C* The precompiler inserts the SQLCA into the input
     C* specifications itself, so INCLUDE SQLCA is accepted but
     C* redundant. Its fields, SQLCOD and the rest, are ordinary
     C* program fields rather than reserved words.
     C/EXEC SQL INCLUDE SQLCA
     C/END-EXEC
     C*
     C* Host variables carry a leading colon.
     C/EXEC SQL SELECT CUSNAM, CUSBAL
     C+ INTO :CUSTNM, :CUSTBL
     C+ FROM CUSTMAST
     C+ WHERE CUSNBR = :CUSNBR
     C/END-EXEC
     C*
     C* Update, insert and delete.
     C/EXEC SQL UPDATE CUSTMAST
     C+ SET CUSBAL = CUSBAL + :ORDAMT
     C+ WHERE CUSNBR = :CUSNBR
     C/END-EXEC
     C/EXEC SQL INSERT INTO ORDHDR
     C+ (ORDNBR, CUSNBR, ORDAMT)
     C+ VALUES (:ORDNBR, :CUSNBR, :ORDAMT)
     C/END-EXEC
     C/EXEC SQL DELETE FROM ORDDTL
     C+ WHERE ORDNBR = :ORDNBR
     C/END-EXEC
     C*
     C* A cursor, with SQL comments inside the statement.
     C/EXEC SQL DECLARE ORDCSR CURSOR FOR
     C+ SELECT ORDNBR, ORDAMT      -- header only
     C+ FROM ORDHDR
     C+ WHERE ORDDAT >= :FROMDT
     C+ ORDER BY ORDNBR
     C/END-EXEC
     C/EXEC SQL OPEN ORDCSR
     C/END-EXEC
     C           FETCHL    TAG
     C/EXEC SQL FETCH ORDCSR INTO :ORDNBR, :ORDAMT
     C/END-EXEC
     C           SQLCOD    COMP 100                      90
     C                     Z-ADDSQLCOD    WRKCOD  50
     C           SQLSTT    MOVE           WRKSTT
     C*
     C* The SQLCA fields in every position they can occupy. A six
     C* character name fills factor 1, factor 2 or the result field
     C* exactly, so it butts against whatever follows.
     C                     Z-ADD*ZERO     SQLCOD           result field
     C           *BLANKS   MOVE           SQLSTT
     C           SQLERR,3  COMP *ZERO                    91
     C           SQLWN0    MOVE           WRKWRN
     C           SQLERM    MOVEL          WRKMSG
     C                     Z-ADDSQLERL    WRKLEN
     C           SQLWNA    MOVE           WRKFLG
     C*
     C* The line below cannot compile: SQLCOD is already defined by
     C* the SQLCA, so giving it a length is a duplicate definition.
     C* It is here because a three digit length fills positions
     C* 49-51 and leaves no separator after the name, which is the
     C* case that a trailing word boundary used to miss.
     C                     Z-ADD*ZERO     SQLCOD256
     C           SQLCOD    CABEQ100       FETCHE
     C                     GOTO FETCHL
     C           FETCHE    TAG
     C/EXEC SQL CLOSE ORDCSR
     C/END-EXEC
     C*
     C* WHENEVER branches to an RPG TAG label.
     C/EXEC SQL WHENEVER SQLERROR GOTO ERRTAG
     C/END-EXEC
     C/EXEC SQL WHENEVER NOT FOUND CONTINUE
     C/END-EXEC
     C*
     C* Operators. The -- that opens a comment must not read as two
     C* minus signs, and the slash of a qualified name is not
     C* division.
     C/EXEC SQL SELECT * FROM PAYLIB/CUSTMAST
     C+ WHERE CUSBAL >= :LOWBAL
     C+ AND CUSBAL <= :HIGHBAL
     C+ AND CUSTYP <> 'X'
     C+ AND CUSNBR = :CUSNBR
     C+ AND CUSDUE > CUSPAY
     C+ AND CUSAGE < 90
     C+ AND CUSBAL * 2 + CUSFEE - CUSCR > 0
     C+ AND CUSRTE / 12 <= 100
     C+ AND FIRSTN || LASTN <> ''      -- concatenation
     C+ AND CUSNAM <> 'O''BRIEN'       -- doubled quote
     C+ AND CUSFLG = X'F1'
     C+ AND CUSNOT <> 'a -- b is not a comment'
     C+ AND CUSRTE = 12.75
     C+ AND CUSADJ = -3.5
     C+ AND CUST1 > 0             -- digits in a name
     C+ FETCH FIRST 10 ROWS ONLY
     C/END-EXEC
     C*
     C* A function call, and one of the SQL global variables.
     C/EXEC SQL SELECT SUM(CUSBAL), MAX(CUSDUE)
     C+ INTO :TOTBAL, :MAXDUE
     C+ FROM CUSTMAST
     C+ WHERE UPPER(CUSNAM) = :CUSNAM
     C/END-EXEC
     C/EXEC SQL SET :JOBNAM = JOB_NAME
     C/END-EXEC
     C/EXEC SQL VALUES CLIENT_IPADDR INTO :CLIENT
     C/END-EXEC
     C/EXEC SQL COMMIT
     C/END-EXEC
     C/EXEC SQL ROLLBACK
     C/END-EXEC
     C           ERRTAG    TAG
     C           'SQL BAD' DSPLY*EXT
     C                     SETON                         LR
     C*
     C* A page and line number in 1-5 does not disturb an embedded
     C* SQL statement, its continuation lines, or its terminator.
08010C/EXEC SQL SELECT CUSNAM
08020C+ INTO :CUSTNM
08030C+ FROM CUSTMAST
08040C+ WHERE CUSNBR = :CUSNBR AND CUSBAL > 0
08050C/END-EXEC
08060C           SQLCOD    COMP 0                        92
